.TH WLCROSSHAIR 1 "2026-08-24" "wlcrosshair 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wlcrosshair \- crosshair overlay for Wayland compositors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlcrosshair
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wlcrosshair
is a minimal crosshair overlay for Wayland compositors that support the
wlr-layer-shell protocol (e.g.\& Hyprland, Sway, COSMIC, KDE Plasma).
.PP
It runs as a background daemon, drawing a crosshair image on a layer-shell
surface at the overlay layer, above all other windows including fullscreen
applications and games.  It listens on a Unix socket for commands from
.BR wlcrosshairctl (1).
.PP
The crosshair starts hidden.  Use
.B wlcrosshairctl
to toggle, show, hide, or reload the overlay.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.I ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml
(respects
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
.SS Config Fields
.TP
.BI path " = " PATH
.I (required)
Path to a PNG crosshair image.  Tilde expansion is supported.
.TP
.BI output " = " NAME
.I (required)
Wayland output name as reported by the compositor (e.g.\&
.BR DP-1 ,
.BR eDP-1 ,
.BR HDMI-A-1 ).
Use
.B hyprctl monitors
to find yours.
.TP
.BI size " = " PIXELS
.I (required if width/height not set)
Set both width and height to this value.
.TP
.BI width " = " PIXELS
.I (required if size not set)
Width of the crosshair in pixels.
.TP
.BI height " = " PIXELS
.I (required if size not set)
Height of the crosshair in pixels.
.SS Example Config
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
path = "~/.config/wlcrosshair/crosshair.png"
output = "DP-1"
size = 24
.fi
.RE
.SH SOCKET
.B wlcrosshair
listens on
.I /tmp/crosshair.sock
for IPC commands (one per line).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the config directory.  Defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml
Default configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wlcrosshairctl (1)
